From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:17:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix span backgrounds, select labels and image source
 selection

This bundles four small fixes to the baseline patch:

- Inline span backgrounds: the background brush was never set, so a
  span with a background color but no padding or border produced no
  decoration fragment and its background was not painted. A visible
  (non-transparent) background color now sets the brush to the span's
  node id; paint still resolves the color from that node.
- Closed <select> labels: the label only looked at direct <option>
  children. It now walks options in tree order, including those inside
  <optgroup>. The last selected option wins for a single select and the
  first for a multiple one. With no selected option, a single select
  with size <= 1 shows the first enabled option, honouring disabled
  options and disabled groups, before falling back to the first option.
- <picture> sources: only image/avif was skipped, so a source of any
  other format this build cannot decode (for example image/jxl) hid a
  later supported source or the <img> fallback. A source is now used
  only when its type, ignoring case and parameters, is PNG, JPEG, GIF,
  WebP, or SVG when the svg feature is on.
- srcset descriptors: a bad descriptor counted as 1x, NaN and infinity
  were accepted, and large widths went through f64. Descriptors now
  follow the HTML rules: invalid candidates are skipped, density uses
  the HTML number syntax and must be finite and positive, a height is
  accepted only with a width, and widths compare as decimal text so they
  cannot overflow. The largest candidate still wins, and width
  descriptors still beat density ones in a mixed list.
